 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-idp1983504\" class=\"interactive\" data-label=\"\">\n<h3 class=\"os-title\" data-type=\"title\">\n  <span class=\"os-title-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h3>\n<div class=\"os-note-body\">\n<h4 data-type=\"title\" id=\"7\" class=\"os-subtitle\">\n  <span class=\"os-subtitle-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h4>\n<span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idp138735392\" data-alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20220509.174553/resources/fe2f00723c4e1fc22f998e16d5bc74f2cbb45c26\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\" width=\"120\" id=\"8\">\n</span>\n<p id=\"fs-idm45931344\">Go to this <a href=\"https://openstaxcollege.org/l/genetic_drift\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">site</a> to watch an animation of random sampling and genetic drift in action.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 233580,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Compare and contrast the bottleneck and founder effects.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 724468,
     "content_html": "Both the bottleneck and founder effect are examples of gene flow. However, the bottleneck effect occurs after a cataclysmic event, whereas the founder effect occurs when mutations introduce new alleles into a population."
    },
    {
     "id": 724471,
     "content_html": "Both the bottleneck and founder effect are examples of genetic drift. However, the bottleneck effect is a process in which a large portion of a genome is wiped out, whereas the founder effect occurs when members of a larger population migrate to establish their own population."
    },
    {
     "id": 724469,
     "content_html": "Both the bottleneck and founder effect change the genetic structure of a population. However, the bottleneck effect reduces or eliminates alleles within a population, whereas the founder effect introduces or increases alleles."
    },
    {
     "id": 724470,
     "content_html": "Both the bottleneck and founder effect change the genetic structure of a population. However, the bottleneck effect occurs when inbreeding depression kills off part of a population, whereas the founder effect relies on nonrandom mating."
    }
   ],
